implementationPlan.description:
scripts/moe-agent.sh: under the strong profile, only a verified completion may move the target (DoD 1).

First read the LANDED CQ-V07 (task-16bbf8ff) and CQ-V08 (task-2720c13b) bytes: PINNED_ATTEMPT_PROFILE, the intent journal and its refusal path, and receipt_journal_fields with profile and treeSha. Adapt to their landed names. Keep every peer's bytes; this file is a collision hotspot (ad0dc2e7, c2a900aa, bc8410af, bdf6db6f).

(a) Add a helper, strong_landing_task TASKID. It is true when ANY of these says 'verified-local':
- PINNED_ATTEMPT_PROFILE, when TASKID is this session's pinned task;
- the executionPolicySnapshot.profile of the task's NEWEST readable attempt record (highest generation) in .moe/attempts/*.json, which the daemon writes. Reuse moe_attempt_read's $PYTHON_CMD reader style. An unreadable record is skipped, never trusted;
- a receipt journal for TASKID whose own profile is verified-local.
The helper never reads an environment variable a CLI can set.

(b) The gate: in run_landing, right AFTER the landing_owner_guard check (about line 5401) and before anything reads or writes bytes, the baseline or refs. When LAND_KIND is checkpoint and strong_landing_task "$LAND_TASK_ID" is true, refuse with LAND_CODE MOE_COMMIT_REFUSED_STRONG_CHECKPOINT, through a landing_refuse_strong helper shaped like landing_refuse_owner (about line 3472):
- set LAND_OUTCOME='refused';
- print a [WARN] naming the code, the task and the branch, and saying the bytes and baseline stay for the verified completion;
- call record_commit_rpc with refused and the code;
- fill the session-ended summary with outcome=refused and the code;
- set MOE_LANDING_DONE=true;
- write NO update-ref, NO rescue ref, NO baseline change and NO temp index.

This one gate covers every checkpoint path, because all of them go through run_landing:
- the post-flight exit checkpoint (LAND_KIND=$LANDING_MODE, about line 8596);
- the pre-flight recovery (about line 5762, including a gate-failed strong completion's rescued bytes, whose rescue ref stays as it is);
- the idle-path recoveries.
The Ctrl+C teardown rescue (LAND_KIND=rescue) only writes a rescue ref, so it is unchanged.

This step's error handling: strong fails closed only for a task some trusted record names verified-local. With no such record, every landing is byte-for-byte today's behavior, including the existing recovery messages.

scripts/moe-agent.sh: a strong receipt journal now lives until finalize is acknowledged (DoD 2, CQ-V08's handed-forward residual).

Why: receipt_send (about line 5215) deletes the journal on an accepted receipt BEFORE finalize_attempt is sent. A crash between the two leaves the attempt finalizing with no journal. The daemon keeps a finalizing attempt's hold across restarts (packages/moe-daemon/src/state/attemptStore.ts reconcileRunningAttempts), so nothing would ever close it. The task is wedged in REVIEW: claims and qa_approve are refused.

The change applies ONLY to a journal whose own profile is verified-local. Legacy and observe journals keep today's deletion:

(a) receipt_send, on an accepted receipt:
- set a per-call RECEIPT_ACKED=true;
- KEEP a strong journal;
- on DELIVERY_RECEIPT_CONFLICT, keep CQ-V08's handling, which deletes the journal and treats the receipt as acknowledged;
- reset RECEIPT_ACKED at each call.

(b) finalize_postflight, CQ-V08's strong deferral:
- key 'receipt unacknowledged' on RECEIPT_ACKED (or LAND_PROOF_UNTRANSFERRED) instead of the journal still existing;
- when a strong committed landing is acknowledged, send finalize_attempt_rpc landed;
- delete RECEIPT_JOURNAL only after that RPC succeeds;
- on failure keep it and print the existing exhausted warning, so the next pre-flight replay finishes it.

(c) receipt_replay, about line 5318, for a strong journal after receipt_send acknowledged it:
- if the journaled attempt is still finalizing, send finalize 'landed' with the same tree that CQ-V08 (d) already checks. Delete the journal on success; keep it, with the existing warning, on failure;
- a closed attempt deletes the journal, since nothing is left to acknowledge;
- running, reconciling or mismatch keeps it, with a [WARN] naming the attempt and phase.

V08 (a)'s MOE_COMMIT_REFUSED_UNRECONCILED_INTENT still refuses a new strong completion while that journal exists. So a kept journal can never lead to a second landing.

Use only the existing helpers (receipt_journal_path, receipt_journal_fields, moe_pinned_attempt_phase, finalize_attempt_rpc, moe_evidence_rpc). Add no new state file and no new journal field.

scripts/moe-agent.ps1 is the exact twin of steps 1 and 2, in string parity: the same code MOE_COMMIT_REFUSED_STRONG_CHECKPOINT, the same banners, env names and settings names.

Twins:
- the strong_landing_task helper reads $script:PinnedAttemptProfile (CQ-V07), the newest readable .moe/attempts record of the task (Read-MoeAttempt's reader style, about line 1558) and a strong journal (Get-MoeReceiptJournalPath, about line 2711);
- the gate goes in Invoke-MoeLanding (about line 4476), right after its Get-MoeOwnerGuard refusal, and has the same refusal shape;
- the recovery's Invoke-MoeLanding -Kind 'checkpoint' (about line 5018) and the post-flight $moeMode checkpoint (about lines 7533 and 7538) reach it unchanged;
- the journal lifetime: Send-MoeReceipt (about line 1707), Complete-MoePostflight (about line 5167) with Send-MoeFinalize (about line 1749), and Invoke-MoeReceiptReplay (about line 1840).

Keep the file UTF-8 with a BOM, which Windows PowerShell 5.1 needs, and every peer's bytes. Then run `bash scripts/tests/parity-check.sh`, and its .ps1 sibling when pwsh is available. Register the new code there only if the check keeps an explicit list.

scripts/tests/postflight.sh: add three modes to the embedded frozen-candidate suite. The same JS also lives in postflight.ps1; step 5 keeps the two copies byte-identical.

Reuse:
- CQ-V07's strong fixture: the .moe/attempts record with executionPolicySnapshot {version:2, profile:'verified-local', planRevision, deliveryPolicy:'local-branch'}, the frozen gate candidate, and the regular file at <gitdir>/moe/receipt for unwritable;
- CQ-V08's receipt machinery: the fake daemon's receipt answers, the receipt-held crash supervisor, the FAKE_CLAIM_MODE 'finalizing' second runs and the RPC call log.

Each mode asserts exact codes, the order of calls in the log, the wrapper's exit status and Git state (`git rev-parse` of the branch and `git for-each-ref refs/moe/rescue`), and prints stdout and stderr on failure. A mode is never skipped silently.

1. strong-checkpoint-held (post-flight):
   - a strong session exits WORKING with dirty owned bytes;
   - it is refused with MOE_COMMIT_REFUSED_STRONG_CHECKPOINT;
   - the branch ref is byte-identical; no new refs/moe/rescue/*; the worktree bytes and baseline file are byte-identical;
   - record_commit carries outcome refused with the code, and the session line reads outcome=refused code=MOE_COMMIT_REFUSED_STRONG_CHECKPOINT;
   - the variant sets a CLI-visible env var claiming profile legacy and must still be refused.
2. strong-recovery-held (pre-flight):
   - run 1 is CQ-V07's unwritable strong completion (refused; bytes and baseline kept);
   - run 2 makes the receipt dir writable again, and its pre-flight recovery is refused with the same code;
   - the branch is byte-identical and there is NO MOE_CHECKPOINT_RECOVERED line;
   - a second variant starts from a gate-failed strong completion: its refs/moe/rescue/<task>/* ref still exists, unmoved, after run 2.
3. reconcile-strong-finalize-lost:
   - run 1: a strong landing succeeds and record_delivery_receipt is accepted, then finalize_attempt is lost (the fake daemon drops it, or the crash supervisor kills the wrapper right after the accepted receipt);
   - expect exactly one Moe-Kind: completion commit, and the journal KEPT;
   - run 2, a finalizing claim: the replay re-sends the identical receipt (answered as accepted), THEN finalize 'landed' with landedRevision = targetAfter, in that order and exactly once;
   - expect still one completion commit, the branch unchanged by run 2, and the journal gone.

Every existing receipt-*, intent-* and reconcile-strong-* mode must pass UNCHANGED. If one of them asserts the very residual being fixed (a strong journal deleted before finalize is acknowledged), stop and report it in complete_step. Never edit it silently.

VERIFY ONCE, fresh.

1. The DoD command, `bash scripts/tests/postflight.sh`, runs the full suite: the three new modes plus every existing mode. It must exit 0. Supply its command, exit code and output tail to complete_task. Widen MOE_POSTFLIGHT_TIMEOUT_SEC on a busy box; a timeout is diagnosed, never retried into green.
2. ALSO run these, and report each result in the completion summary:
   - `bash scripts/tests/parity-check.sh` (and its .ps1 sibling when pwsh exists);
   - postflight.ps1 under pwsh, and under PowerShell 5.1 when reachable;
   - `node --test scripts/tests/prompt-cache-launcher.test.mjs scripts/tests/agent-runtime.test.mjs scripts/tests/resume-progress.test.mjs`, the V07/V08 DoD command, to prove nothing else regressed.
3. Mutants, applied to scratch copies of the wrappers, never the shared files. Each must turn its named mode red; restore, cmp, and rerun green:
   (i) gate only recoveries (LAND_RECOVERED) -> strong-checkpoint-held;
   (ii) read strong from the env var instead of the pinned or record source -> the strong-checkpoint-held env variant;
   (iii) delete the strong journal on an accepted receipt, today's behavior -> reconcile-strong-finalize-lost run 2;
   (iv) finalize before re-sending the receipt in the replay -> the order assertion;
   (v) refuse every checkpoint regardless of profile -> the existing legacy recovery modes.
